eveloping bishop to c4 targeting f7.  \n- **Nc3** (N: b1-c3): Develops knight, supports d5 push later.  \n- **f5-f6**: A speculative pawn sac to open Black’s king position? Black’s pawn on g7 is still there, so f6 might be met by ...gxf6, opening g-file but weakening Black’s king cover. However, it’s premature as White hasn’t developed pieces fully.  \n\nReason: In the opening, quick development and king safety are key. **N: g1-f3** is a standard, solid developing move that controls e5 and d4, prepares castling, and keeps options open. Alternatives like d4-d5 are also good for space, but it’s a bit early before all pieces are developed.  \n\nAnswer: N: g1-f3"}
