 here. Castling (e1-g1) immediately secures the king, connects rooks, and prepares for a middlegame where White can use the central pawn tension and piece activity to launch an attack. Moving the knight (e7-d5) is tempting but leaves the king exposed and misses the chance to castle quickly. Given Black’s king is also uncastled, delaying castling could lead to dangerous tactics. So castling now is the most solid and best practical choice.\n\n**Answer:** K: e1-g1'}
