*P: f2-f4** – advances pawn, but doesn’t exploit the tactical opportunity right now.\n\n**Reason:**  \nN: e6-c7 is the most forcing and likely winning move: it attacks the black king and the black bishop simultaneously. Black has no good squares for the king that avoid material loss. If Kc8 or Ke8, Nxd5 wins bishop. If K moves elsewhere, bishop still attacked and we may win it or deliver check with discovered attacks. This maximizes pressure, likely wins a piece, and improves White’s position decisively.\n\n**Answer:** N: e6-c7'}
