 g1-g2** – Improves king safety, centralizes slightly.  \n\n**Reason:**  \n**N: c7-e6** is the most forcing and gains material immediately—it attacks Black’s king (e7) and Black’s bishop (d8) at the same time. Black cannot defend both, so White will win the bishop. Additionally, it puts the knight in a more active position for further attacks on Black’s king. Other moves either don’t create immediate threats or miss this clear tactical opportunity.  \n\n**Answer:** N: c7-e6'}
